    "description": "Valor Compute Infrastructure is an investment vehicle created to acquire and lease data center compute infrastructure used in AI workloads. The platform serves large-scale digital infrastructure demand through an asset-heavy leasing model rather than through conventional retail colocation or managed hosting services. Apollo stated in January 2026 that VCI was part of a $5.4 billion transaction to acquire and lease NVIDIA GB200 GPU infrastructure to an xAI subsidiary under a triple-net structure. The disclosed scale makes the platform a specialized owner-lessor of high-value compute equipment tied to next-generation data center demand. Apollo announced that it led a $3.5 billion capital solution for VCI in January 2026, while public sources do not disclose the current ownership percentages within the vehicle.",
